    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **34 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp23Tests` (GOLD tier) and the existing `Cp15Tests` (SILVER/BRONZE) and household tests (`Cp11`, `Cp13`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` is derived at read time in `OwnerMapper` from the `Owner`. To add the GOLD rule, I gave the mapper the household member count and prioritized it ahead of the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient` `householdSize` field (with getter/setter). It's computed on read rather than persisted, so the tier reflects the current household.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` expression now returns `\"GOLD\"` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls back to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE rule.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `populateHouseholdSize(Owner)`, which counts owners sharing the same `householdId` (an owner with no `householdId` is a household of one), and called it before mapping in `getOwner`, `listOwners`, and the create response of `addOwner`.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` field description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nThe GOLD determination counts owners by shared `householdId`. Since the create flow already backfills a common `householdId` onto every existing household member, the third member (and the whole household) correctly resolves to a household size of 3 and reports GOLD on read.",
